  "query_preview": "..\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nBlocking Hudson Bay low maintains cyclonic northwest flow across\nthe northern plains through the period. Flow buckles today,\nbringing increased influence from western heat dome, and\nincreasing temperatures into northeast Montana. Some compressional\nheating will also contribute to warming with downslope flow ahead\nof a shortwave diving through the northwest flow. \n\nWith the well mixed atmosphere and mid-level forcing with the\nshortwave and circulation along a frontal boundary, could see \nscattered thunderstorms with the potential for hail and strong to \nsevere winds during the late afternoon to evening. \n\nMixing in the afternoon followed by cold air advection behind the\nshortwave, will increase winds enough to reach Lake Wind Criteria\nby this afternoon, with winds increasing overnight into Wednesday.\n\nAdditional storms are expected on Wednesday with another but\nweaker shortwave.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nPops through Wednesday were blended with the latest CAMS. NBM has\nbeen too dry lately with this cyclonic NW flow.\n\nThe rest of the forecast used the NBM.",
